concept:aged-care-legislation-amendment-increasing-consumer-choice-act-2016-sch-1-sec-20 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20 Before section 9-1"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-20 ;
    values:originalText "Insert: 9-1A  Obligation to notify Secretary about home care services  (1) An approved provider must notify the Secretary of the following information in relation to each home care service through which the approved provider proposes to provide home care:  (a) the name and address of the service;  (b) any other information of a kind specified in the Approved Provider Principles for the purposes of this section. Note: Approved providers have a responsibility under Part 4.3 to comply with this obligation. Failure to comply with a responsibility can result in a sanction being imposed under Part 4.4.  Schedule 1  Amendments" ;
    skos:definition "Insert: 9-1A  Obligation to notify Secretary about home care services  (1) An approved provider must notify the Secretary of the following information in relation to each home care service through which the approved provider proposes to provide home care:  (a) the name and address of the service;  (b) any other information of a kind specified in the Approved Provider Principles for the purposes of this section. Note: Approved providers have a responsibility under Part 4.3 to comply with this obligation. Failure to comply with a responsibility can result in a sanction being imposed under Part 4.4.  Schedule 1  Amendments"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f3baa536cf9f0ddd77275a824095f83a7d8f801349dbb0430a6d4212002b0f31" ;
    cof:pageNumber "11"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Notify Secretary about home care services" ;
    dc:description "Yes" ;
